\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 23\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 -24\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Orationes diversae I
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Domine sancte pater omnipotens, eterne deus, precamur te in nomine dilecti filii tui, domini nostri Ihesu Christi, per quem omnia facta sunt in celo et in terra \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (24\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 O Ihesu Christe, eterna dulcedo te amancium\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Nachtr\u228 \'e4ge von zwei H\u228 \'e4nden, m\u246 \'f6glicherweise auf urspr\u252 \'fcnglich frei gebliebenen Bll. von Lage 2. \endash  Edition: (Nr. 1) Virginia \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Brown\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Flores psalmorum and Orationes psalmodicae in Beneventan Script, in: Terra sancti benedicti. Studies in the Palaeography, History and Liturgy of Medieval Southern Italy. Rom 2005 (Storia e letteratura 219), S. 549-608, hier S. 577 Nr. 86. \endash  (Nr. 2) Claes \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Gejrot\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , The Fifteen Oes: Latin and Vernacular Versions. With an Edition of the Latin Text, in: The Translation of the Works of St Birgitta of Sweden into the Medieval European Vernaculars, hrsg. von Bridget \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Morris\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  / Veronica \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 O\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 \rquote \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Mara\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Turnholt 2000 (The Medieval Translator 7), S. 213-238, Edition S. 223f. Nr. 1.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 25\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 -30\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Orationes ante eucharistiam I
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Omnipotens sempiterne deus, qui propter nimiam rationabilemque dileccionem \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 nec non liberacionem anime mee ab omni dyabolica potestate\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (25\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Omnipotens et mitissime deus, qui de indignis dignos, de inmundis mundos, de peccatoribus iustos facis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 qui est verus et eternus pontifex et solus sine peccati macula sacerdos Jhesus Christus, filius tuus, dominus noster, qui tecum viuit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 3\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (26\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Deus eterne, pater, alpha et o\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [mega],\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  qui ab inicio recentis seculi ad Abel et munera eius misericorditer respexisti\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 et propiciacio fieret ipse pro nobis sacerdos et hostia est effectus, qui tecum in vnitate eiusdem spiritus sancti vivit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (28\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Fortissime deus, spirituum vniuerse carnis donator, domine deus misericors et clemens et patiens et multe misericordie et verus creator omnium, terribilis, fortis et iustus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 et offert in omni bono, quid ipse est in sua diuina natura et sacra humanitate\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 5\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (28\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Svscipe ergo, dulcissime pater, dilecti sobolis preciosam animam in cruce de sacratissimo corpore suo egressam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 quod omnis conuersacio nostra nichil aliud sit quam expressio diuine nature ac execucio conuersacionis domini nostri Ihesu Christi, qui uiuit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 6\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (30\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Obsecro te, domine Ihesu Christe, per viscera misericordie tue, quibus nos visitasti oriens ex alto, vt mihi indignissimo famulo tuo aperire digneris hodie sinum pietatis tue\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 et miseracione in illa hora et in omni tempore necessitatis mee anime et vite mee\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 (Nr. 2) Vgl. Victor \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Leroquais\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , L\rquote ordo Missae du sacramentaire d\rquote Amiens. Paris, Bibl. nat. ms. lat., 9432 (IX\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 e\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  s.), in: Ephemerides Liturgicae 41 = N.S. 1 (1927), S. 435-445, hier S. 440f.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 30\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 -35\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Orationes ante eucharistiam II
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Rogo te, domine Ihesu Christe, fili dei per gloriam sacratissime passionis, ut hodie introducas animam meam in cellam tue dulcissime dileccioni\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 s \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 veni virginis filius et virginum decor et corona\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (35\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : H\u228 \'e4ndewechsel und Beginn einer neuen Lage, ohne Textverlust; Druck: Bl. 30\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Z. 24) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 impone langwenti anime mee tuas paternas manus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ut in tuo amore dulcissimo possim habere plenam leticiam et gaudium sempiternum. Amen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Nicolaus de Saliceto, Antidotarius animae; Druck: GW M39510 = BSB-Ink S-19, Bl. 28\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 -30\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 va\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  Z. 7.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 35\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 -36\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Orationes ante eucharistiam III
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Alia oratio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Domine Ihesu Christe, fili dei viui, qui de hoc mundo transisti ad patrem et dilexisti tuos, qui erat in mundo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 et ab humana derisione et eterna confusione et particeps eterne uite merear fieri\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (35\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Alia oratio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Redempcionis mee singulare principium sumpturus, obsecro te, domine Ihesu Christe, redemptor piissime, ne hoc passionis tue sacramentum in me fiat ociosum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 cum cordis puritate et lacrimarum fonte cum reuerencia et tremore, ut sit tibi laus et honor nobis salus et remedium. Amen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 3\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (36\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Alia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Obsecro te, piissime redemptor mundi, per sacrosanctum corpus et sanguinem tuum, ut non digneris me repellere a communione tanti misterii\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 et oratio mea exaudiatur in excelso polo glorie tue et ut ad gaudia eterna merear peruenire te adiuuante\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (36\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Alia oratio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Adoro, domine Jhesu Christe, sanctissimum corpus tuum, quod hodie consecrauit per totum mundum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 rescita carne et sangwine nostris oculis corporalibus sub modica panis et vini specie velata, ut concedas michi miser\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [r]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 imo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 (Nr. 4) Parallel\u252 \'fcberlieferung: Canberra, National Library of Australia, Ms 8, 115\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 ; vgl. Descriptive Catalogue of Medieval and Renaissance Western Manuscripts in Australia, ed. Keith Val \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Sinclair\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Sydney 1969, S. 29.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 37\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 -48\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Orationes ante eucharistiam IV
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 Textbeginn defekt, ein Bl. herausgeschnitten: ||-\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 rimo peccatori illud sacratissimum tuum corpus sumere paruam confessionem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 contra langwiores\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!, recte languores) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ardor amoris tui perseuerancia in bonis operibus corona eterne glorie. Amen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (37\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Consciencia culpabilis vite t\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [r]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 epidus et anxius criminumque funibus captiuatus te\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 3\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (38\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Domine Iesv Christe, fili dei viui, miserere mihi peccatori pleno miseriis et viciis cum omnibus seruis tuis, qui tibi hodie sacratissimum ac preciosum salutis nostre precium sacramentum videlicet corporis et sangwinis tui offerrimus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (39\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 O benigne Iesv Christe, qui te deo patri in ara crucis hostiam vere dignam et vere pacificam pro nobis miseriis et indignis peccatoribus offerre\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 concede mihi hodie sic te suscipere, ut merear tecum sine fine manere. Amen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 5\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (40\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Domine Ihesu Christe, suscipe hoc sacrificium meum in memoria illius summi sacrificii, quo te ipsum obtulisti deo patri pro peccatis meis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 et cum omnibus fidelibus christianis viuis et defunctis nunc et in eternum. Amen. Dirigatur, domine, ad te\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 6\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (41\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Domine Iesv Christe, pastor bone, lumen inextinguibile, pater tocius gracie, qui nobis indignis peccatoribus tantam gratiam dedisti\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 7\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (44\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Pvlcherrime Ihesu, rogo te per illam sacratissimam effusionem preciosissimi sangwinis tui, quo sumo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!, recte sumus) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 redempti\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 8\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (45\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Jtem alia oratio. Ad mensam dulcissimi conuivii tui, domine Ihesu Christe, rex angelorum, ego peccator accessurus vereor et contremisco\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 9\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (46\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Presta mihi, pater omnipotens, ut plena gratia tua et illuminacione sancti spiritus accedam ad sanctum corpus et sangwinem filii tui\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 10\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (47\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Alia oratio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Pota, domine, animam meam de torrente tue voluptatis rigans et inebrians\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 11\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Sic mittit, domine, sacer sangwis tuus, quem bibi in ablucionem peccatorum in refrigerium viciorum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 in gratiarum accione omnium tuorum et beneficiorum et eterna refeccio anime mee. Amen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Transfige, dulcissime Jhesu, medullas anime mee suauissimo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 13\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (48\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Oratio. Indignum me, domine, deus meus, sacrificiis tuis esse fateor, qui innumeris cottidie peccatis obfuscor\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 14\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (48\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Consciencia quidem trepidus, omnipotens deus, ad altare tuum accedo, sed fiduciam de tua pietatis inmensitate retineo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 (Nr. 2) Ps.-Anselmus Cantuariensis, Oratio 32, ed. PL 158, 926AC. \endash  (Nr. 3) Druck: Agendarium, sive ordo rituum et ceremoniarum, ed. Sebastian \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Fuchs\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Bruck an der Teya = Klosterbruck 1595, S. 36-38. \endash  (Nr. 6) Parallel\u252 \'fcberlieferung: Basel, UB, A X 94, 259\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 ; A X 96, 67\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . \endash  (Nr. 7) Druck: Ps.-Augustinus, Manuale seu libellus de contemplatione Christi, cap. 11, ed. PL 40, 956. \endash  Vgl. auch \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Haimerl\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1 Fr\u246 \'f6mmigkeit, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 S. 102f. Anm. 600. \endash  (Nr. 8) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Wilmart\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Auteurs, S. 381 Anm. 2, Nr. 1; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Haimerl\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1 Fr\u246 \'f6mmigkeit, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 S. 90\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1  Anm. 537, S. 126 Anm. 771; vgl. auch GW M39510 = \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 BSB-Ink S-19,\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1  Bl. 24\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\cf1 rb-va\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1 . \endash  (Nr. 9) \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Parallel\u252 \'fcberlieferung: Trier, StBuStArchiv, Hs. 263/16 8\u176 \'b0, 52\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 .\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1  \endash  (Nr. 10) \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Parallel\u252 \'fcberlieferung: Mainz, StB, Hs I 312, 30\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . \endash  (Nr. 12) Edition: Stimulus fratris Jacobi Mediolanensis, ed. PP. Collegii S. Bonaventurae ad Claras Aquas. Quaracchi 1905 (Bibliotheca franciscana ascetica medii aevi 4), S. 3-5. \endash  Lit.: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Wilmart\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Auteurs, S. 381 Anm. 2, Nr. 4; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\cf1 Distelbrink, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1 Bonaventurae scripta, S. 196f. Nr. 219\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . \endash  (Nr. 13) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Deshusses\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Sacramentaire 3, S. 266 Nr. 4384\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1 . \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 \endash  (Nr. 14) De antiquis ecclesiae ritibus libri quatuor. Bd. 1,1, ed. Edmond \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Mart\u232 \'e8\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 ne\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Rouen 1700, S. 516.}

