\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 I\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 rv\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (fliegender Vorsatz) \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Lectionarium
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (I\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Bartholomaeus ap. (24.8.) \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ||\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Polimius rex illius prouinicie misit pro eo rogans, ut liberaret\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 filiam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  [eius a demone, quod etiam fecit]. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Tunc rex aurum et argentum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 fecit eum excoriari et ad ultimum decollari\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (Druck: Brev. Nidrosiense, Bl. tt iii\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Z. 32-tt iiii\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 va\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Z. 15)\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 . \endash  \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Ludewici regis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 \u8249 \'8b (25.8.) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Beatus Ludewicus ex illustribus parentibus natus, pie ix Ludewico rege Francorum christianissimo matre Blanca, quondam regis Castelle filia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 puer in manibus matris proprie cepit gemere et statim restitutus est pristine sanitati\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (teils unleserlich durch Klebespuren; vgl. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Gaposchkin\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , S. 168-176; daran miracula, vgl. ebd. S. 82-88; vgl. auch BHL 5043). \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Beati Augustini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 \u8249 \'8b (28.8.) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Augustinus ex prouincia Africa a Carthaginiensibus parentibus christianis genitus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ad se ingredi nunc tantum medicos et refectionem ministrantes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 . \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 IX\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 \u8249 \'8b \u8230 \'85|| (vgl. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 Brev. Nidrosiense, Bl. tt v\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -tt vi\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ; \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 BHL 785; PL 32, 33-64)\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  (I\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Decollatio Johannis bapt. (29.8.) ||\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 pagani sepulcrum eius invadunt, ossa spargunt et rursus collecta et cremata lacius dispergunt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 adeptus est paupertate fugata\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Druck: Brev. Nidrosiense, Bl. tt vi\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  vorletzte Zeile-tt vii\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Z. 4); (Z. 14-19) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Cum autem post multum temporis Marcellus presbyter\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 translatum est autem capud\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 eius regnante Pipino, rege Francorum, ad Callias\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!, recte Gallias) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 in regionem Equitanie\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!, recte Aquitanie). \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 In natiuitate beate uirginis Marie\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 \u8249 \'8b (8.9.) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Hec est sancta et venerabilis virgo Maria, mater domini secundum carnem, ex semine Abrahe orta\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 cum ipso speciosa virgo fugit in Egyptum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Ps.-Ildefonsus, Sermo dubius 4 de assumptione BMV, PL 96, 258BC; vgl. auch \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Urfels-Capot\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , S. 356 Nr. 122.1-3). \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Infra octauas\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 \u8249 \'8b (15.9.) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Sit nobis tamquam in ymagine descripta vita Marie\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 fugere iactanciam, rationem sequi, amare virtutem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Ambrosius Mediolanensis, De virginibus, lib. 2, cap. 2, PL 16, 208C-209A; vgl. auch \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Urfels-Capot\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , S. 353 Nr. 119.1-2). \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 In exaltacione sancte crucis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 \u8249 \'8b (14.9.) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Multorum temporis habente curriculo Cosdroce inpius adeptus erat regnum Persarum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 quod filius Cosdroce pergens iuxta Danubium, cum suo consedit exercitu\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 || (Ed.: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Urfels-Capot\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , S. 360 Nr. 125.1-3).
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Das Fragment, Textualis, wohl Frankreich, Mitte 13. Jh., stammt vermutlich aufgrund der Heiligenfeste aus einem dominikanischen Lectionar. F\u252 \'fcr jedes Fest sind neun \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs20 lectiones\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  vorgesehen, deren Wortlaut Parallelen zum Brev. Nidrosiense sowie zu der Hs. Rom, Santa Sabina XIV L1, dem um 1255/1260 entstandenen Normcodex f\u252 \'fcr die dominikanische Liturgie, aufweisen. \endash  Abgek\u252 \'fcrzte Lit.: Brev. Nidrosiense = Breviarium ad usum ritumque sacrosancte Nidrosiensis ecclesie. Paris: Jean Kerbriant / Jean Bienayse, 1519, ND Oslo 1964 (Digitalisat: https://www.nb.no/items/URN:NBN:no-nb_digibok_2007092813001; digitale Edition: https://www.bokselskap.no/boker/breviarium/titlepage, ed. by Ingrid \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Sperber\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , with an Introduction by Espen \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Karlsen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  / Sigurd \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Hareide\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Oslo 2012); zum Brev. Nidrosiense vgl. Hans \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Buvarp\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  / Baltzer M. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Borsum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Appendix to Breviarium Nidrosiense. Translated by Ragnar I. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Christophersen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Oslo 1964. \endash  Zum dominikanischen Einfluss auf das Brev. Nidrosiense vgl. Gisela \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Attinger\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Some Reflections on the Liturgy for St \u222 \'deorl\u225 \'e1kr, in: Dominican Resonances in Medieval Iceland. The Legacy of Bishop J\u243 \'f3n Halld\u243 \'f3rsson of Sk\u225 \'e1lholt, ed. by Gunnar \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Har\u240 \'f0arson\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  / Karl-Gunnar \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Johansson\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Leiden u.a. 2021 (The Northern World 91), S. 203-221, hier S. 218f. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Gaposchkin\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  = Blessed Louis, the Most Glorious of Kings. Texts Relating to the Cult of Saint Louis of France, ed. by Marianne Cecilia \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Gaposchkin\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Translations with Phyllis B. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Katz\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Notre Dame, Ind. 2012 (Notre Dame Texts in Medieval Culture). \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Urfels-Capot\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  = Le sanctoral du lectionnaire de l'office dominicain (1254-1256). \u201 \'c9dition et \u233 \'e9tude d'apr\u232 \'e8s le ms. Rome, Sainte-Sabine XIV L1 \u8218 \'82Ecclesiasticum officium secundum ordinem fratrum praedicatorum,\lquote ed. Anne-\u201 \'c9lisabeth \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Urfels-Capot\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Paris 2007 (M\u233 \'e9moires et documents 84).}

