\pard\fi0\li0\qc\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 I (Bl. 1-56)
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 -56\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Eclogae tractatorum in Psalterium
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa120\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Im Kopfsteg von j\u252 \'fcngerer Hand: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 super psalterium a psalmo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \u8218 \'82\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Beatus vir\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 \lquote  (Ps 1) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 usque ad psalmum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \u8218 \'82\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Memento domine\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 \lquote  (Ps 131). \endash  Praefatio: ||\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ubi aliquid de ebr\u230 \'e6ica ueritate defuisse radiat. Inter expositores psalmorum de hoc nomine qu\u230 \'e6dam noscitur prouenisse diuersitas\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 histo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [ria] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 autem profetica in psalmis est\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (Ed.: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Verkest\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , S. 288-291 Z. 130-198). \endash  (2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Incipiunt in nomine Ihesu Christi argumenta Hi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [e]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [onimi] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 in psalmis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (korr. aus psalmos). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Argumenta sunt, quae causas ostendunt ex breuitate sermonum longumque sensum habent\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (Ed.: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Verkest\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , S. 291 Z. 198-201). \endash  (Text) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Beatus uir. Moralis psalmus est, quod ex his, quae sequuntur, apparet, in quibus et de uirtutum appetitu et de errorum abstinentia disputatur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 id est manifestata est, quod in campo planitiae, scilicet arie ornae, id est in uertice\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  [montis]|| Textabbruch.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 Textanfang und -ende defekt. \endash  Teiledition: (1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 -3\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 , 21\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 rv\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 , 36\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 rv\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 ) Martin \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 McNamara\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18  / Maurice \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 Sheehy\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 , Psalter Text and Psalter Study in the Early Irish Church (A.D. 600-1200), in: Proceedings of the Royal Irish Academy 73 (1973), S. 201-298, hier S. 285-290; wiederabgedruckt in: Martin \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 McNamara\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 , Introduction to Glossa in Psalmos: The Hiberno-Latin Gloss on the Psalms of Codex Palatinus Latinus 68. Sheffield 2000 (Journal for the Study of the Old Testament. Supplement Series 165), App. III S. 124-131; (1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 -2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 ) Pascal \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 Verkest\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 , The Praefatio of the Irish \u8218 \'82Eglogae tractatorum in psalterium\lquote , Edited with a Critical Introduction, in: Sacris Erudiri 40 (2001), S. 267-292, hier S. 282-291 (vollst\u228 \'e4ndiger Text), vgl. ferner S. 269 (diese Hs. mit Sigle M), S. 273-278 (zu den Textzeugen M und G = St. Gallen, StiftsB, Cod. Sang. 261, S. 147-274, einschlie\u223 \'dflich Stemma codicum). \endash  Lit.: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf1 Stegm\u252 \'fc\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf1 ller, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf1 RB 7, 11035;\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf1 Bischoff\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf1 , Wendepunkte, S. 238 Nr. 6b, ferner S. 217, 219, 222f.; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 McNamara\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 /\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 Sheehy\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 , Psalter Text (s.o. Teiledition), S. 225-227 Nr. 9; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf1 Lapidge/Sharpe\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 , S. 210 Nr. 783; Joseph F. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 Kelly\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 , A Catalogue of Early Medieval Hiberno-Latin Biblical Commentaries (I), in: Traditio 44 (1988), S. 537-571, hier S. 566 Nr. 39 (Hs. genannt); Charles D. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 Wright\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 , Hiberno-Latin and Irish-influenced Biblical Commentaries, Florilegia, and Homily Collections, in: Sources of Anglo-Saxon Literary Culture: A Trial Version, ed. by Frederick M. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 Biggs\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18  u.a. Binghamton 1990 (Medieval and Renaissance Texts and Studies 74), S. 87-123, hier S. 96 Nr. 11; Michael W. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 Herren\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 , Irish Biblical Commentaries before 800, in: Roma, magistra mundi. Itineraria culturae medievalis. M\u233 \'e9langes offerts au P\u232 \'e8re L. E. Boyle \u224 \'e0 l'occasion de son 75\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 e\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18  anniversaire. Bde. 1-3, ed. Jacqueline \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 Hamesse\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 . Louvain-la-Neuve 1998 (Textes et \u233 \'e9tudes du Moyen \u194 \'c2ge 10, 1-3), hier Bd. 1, S. 391-407 [98.58567-1, entliehen FL -21.08.23]; Mark \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 Stanbury\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 , Early-Medieval Biblical Commentaries, in: Fr\u252 \'fchmittelalterliche Studien 33 (1999), S. 49-82, hier S. 75-80, Hs. genannt S. 75; Michael \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 Gorman\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 , The Myth of Hiberno-Latin Exegesis, in: Revue b\u233 \'e9n\u233 \'e9dictine 110 (2000), S. 42-85, zu dieser Hs. S. 64 Nr. 6B, kritische Auseinandersetzung mit Bischoffs Kriterien f\u252 \'fcr die hiberno-lateinischen Kommentare zur Bibelexegese s. S. 42-59; D\u225 \'e1ibh\u237 \'ed \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 Cr\u243 \'f3\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 in\u237 \'ed\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 n\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 , Bischoff's Wendepunkte Fifty Years On, in: Revue b\u233 \'e9n\u233 \'e9dictine 110 (2000), S. 204-237 als Entgegnung auf Gormans Kritik bei affirmativer Bewertung der Kriterien Bischoffs (s. S. 225-230), zu dieser Hs. s. S. 231 Anm. 100; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 McNamara\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 , Introduction to Glossa (s. Ed.), S. 50-52 Nr. 2.9 (Hs. genannt), vgl. ferner S. 90f., 95, 106, 355f., 397-401.}

