\pard\fi0\li0\qc\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 II (Bl. 57-61)
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 57\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 -61\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Sermones de dedicatione ecclesiae (unvollst\u228 \'e4ndig)
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa120\itap0 \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 1\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Sanctificaui domum hanc \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 (III Rg 9,3). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Celebrauit Sal\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [omon] (II Mcc 2,12). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Considerantes quante facte sunt sollempnitates a Moyse in dedicatione tabenaculi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \u8230 \'85 (Johannes de Rupella, \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Schneyer\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , Rep. 3, S. 717 Nr. 199). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 (58\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 va\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Terribilis est locus iste\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (Gn 28,17). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Istud verbum decantatur in officio misse dedicationis ecclesie. Ideo notandum, quod secundum diuinam scripturam legimus quadruplicem locum legimus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (! bis) \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 3\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 (60\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Vidi ciuitatem sanctam Ierusalem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (Apc 21,2). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Sicut dicit beatus Augustinus: Duplex est ciuitas secundum duplicem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  [differentiam] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ciuium, vna est reproborum et alia iustorum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 \u8230 \'85 (Martinus Oppaviensis, \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Schneyer\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , Rep. 4, S. 148 Nr. 317). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 (61\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Platea ciuitatis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (Apc 21,21). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 In festo ascensionis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (!, recte consecrationis) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Ecclesie legitur de ciuitate sancta Ierusalem, de cuius platea uerbum premissum est dictum, in sacra enim scriptura quattuor reperiuntur ciuitates\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 fluuius ille splendidissimus est ewangelica pre-\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 || Textabbruch. \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 5\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 (61\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ) Auf den Blattr\u228 \'e4ndern Nachtrag von anderer Hand (s. auch Kodikologie): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Confitemini alterutrum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (Iac 5,16). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Duabus tantum creaturis deus inimicatur malo angelo et malo homini in tantum, quod utrique semper ardebunt in inferno\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 generaliter debet confiteri\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 || Textabbruch, Fortsetzung auf dem ersten Steg des beschnittenen Quaternios erkennbar (Bertholdus Ratisbonensis, Rusticanus de sanctis, \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Schneyer\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , Rep. 1, S. 482f. Nr. 132).
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 (Nr. 1-4) Parallel\u252 \'fcberlieferung: Eichst\u228 \'e4tt, UB, Cod. st 348, 110\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 -117\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18  Nr. 1-4; Melk, StiftsB, Cod. 516, 79\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 ra-\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 83\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18  Nr. 1-4; vgl. auch Frankfurt/Main, UB J. C. Senckenberg, Ms. Praed. 35, 166\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 -170\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 ; Uppsala, UB, C 351, 186\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 -192\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18  (jeweils mit abweichender Reihenfolge). \endash  (Nr. 1) Vgl. auch Kilian F. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 Lynch\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 , A List of the Sermons of John de Rupella, in: \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf1 Recherches de th\u233 \'e9ologie ancienne et m\u233 \'e9di\u233 \'e9vale 31 (1964), S. 287-319, hier S. 318 (Schluss abweichend)\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf18 .}

