\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 83\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 -84\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Collectio sententiarum patrum latinorum
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa120\itap0 \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 (Z. 12) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 De abstinentia. Johannes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Item\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  [n]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 on est abstinencia reputanda, ubi ventris ingluuies fuerit subsecuta\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (vgl. Isidorus Hispalensis, Sententiae 2.44.10, CCL 111, ed. Pierre \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Cazier\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , S. 192 Z. 55-57) \u8230 \'85; \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 (Z. 19) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 De accedia. Augustinus: O si possemus excitare homines et cum illis pariter excitari, ut tales essemus amatores uite permanentis, quales sumus amatores uite fugientis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (In Iohannis euangelium tractatus 49, CCL 36, ed. Radbodus \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Willems\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , S. 420 \u167 \'a7 2 Z. 18-20) \u8230 \'85; \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 3\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 (Z. 25) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 De adulacione. Augustinus: Hec est ira dei magna, ut desit oratio et assit adulacio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (Bruno Herbipolensis, Expositio psalmorum, Ps 9,23, PL 142, 73A) \u8230 \'85; \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 (Z. 28) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 De amicicia. Proverbia: Vir amicabilis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ad societatem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \u8230 \'85 (Prv 18,24). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Tullius\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Maximum est in amicicia superiorem subesse inferiori\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (vgl. Cicero, Laelius de amicitia, cap. 69) \u8230 \'85; \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 5\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 (Z. 32) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 De auaricia. Augustinus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Domine, per auariciam meam amittere te nolui, sed uolui te cum mendacio possidere, ita\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  [quod] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 te amisi, quia non dignaris cum mendacio possideri\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (Confessiones, lib. 10, cap. 41, CCL 27, ed. Luc \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Verheijen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , S. 191 Z. 5-8). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 6\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 (83\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  Z. 13) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 De castitate. Bernardus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Si\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  [mihi] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 castitatem solus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (expungiert) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ademi, numquam misericordiam tuam peremi? Si ego admisi, vnde\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  [me] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 dampnes, numquid tu amisisti ut salues?\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 7\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 (Z. 30) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 De clericis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 . \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 a\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 Bernardus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 Quomodo credam ei animam meam, qui numquam curam anime sue gessit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 . \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 Bernardus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 Res ecclesiarum res pauperum sunt, sed sacrilega eis crudelitate \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 subripitur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \u8230 \'85 (Salimbene de Adam, Cronica, CCCM 125, ed. Giuseppe Scalia, S. 212 \u167 \'a7 203 Z. 1-4). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 8\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 (84\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 De choreis. Augustinus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Melius est\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  [die] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 dominicali arare vel fodere quam choreas ducere\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (vgl. Enarrationes in Ps 91 \u167 \'a7 2, CCL 39, ed. Eligio \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Dekkers\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  / Jean \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Fraipont\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , S. 1280 Z. 7f.). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 9\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 (Z. 4) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 De cogitatione. Gregorius\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Arguendi sunt, qui cogitaciones a dyabolo inmitti putant et non ex propria uoluntate nasci \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 (Paschasius Radbertus, Expositio in Matheo, lib. 7, CCCM 56A, ed. Beda \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Paulus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , S. 773 Z. 2674f.). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 10\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 (Z. 14) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 De contritione\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 . \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 a\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Augustinus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Plus ualet cordis contricio quam tocius mundi peregrinacio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ; \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Crisostomus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Sic impossibile est, ut ignis inflammetur in aqua\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 \u8230 \'85 illa enim mater fletus, hec est mater risus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (De cordis conpunctione 2.3; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Schmitz\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , S. 25 Z. 26-29); \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 c\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Sola est conpunctio cordis que facit horrescere purpuram\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 amare lacrimas, fugere risum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Schmitz\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , S. 26 Z. 6-8). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 11\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 (Z. 19) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 De obedientia. Bernardus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Verus obediens peccatum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (!, recte mandatum) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 non procrastinat, sed parat aures auditui, linguam voci, manus operi, pedes itineri et se totum intus se\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (! bis) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 colligit, ut mandatum peragat imperantis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 .
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf17 Thematisch geordnete Zusammenstellung patristischer Sentenzen. Aufgef\u252 \'fchrt wird in der Regel nur das erste Zitat. \endash  (Nr. 5) Vgl. auch Meister Eckhart, Sermones de tempore, sermo 24,1, \u167 \'a7 242, in: Meister Eckhart. Die deutschen und lateinischen Werke. Die lateinischen Werke. Bd. 4: Sermones, hrsg. von Ernst \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf17 Benz\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf17  / Bruno \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf17 Decker\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf17  / Josef \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf17 Koch\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf17 . Stuttgart 1956, S. 223 Z. 5-7. \endash  (Nr. 6) Anselmus Cantuariensis, Orationes sive meditationes, Meditatio 2, in: \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf1 Anselmi Cantuariensis archiepiscopi opera omnia. Ed. Franciscus Salesius \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf1 Schmitt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf1 . Bd. 3: Orationes sive meditationes necnon epistolarium librum primum. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf17 Edinburgh\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf17  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf1 1946, S. 82f. Z. 87-89. \endash  (Nr. 7a) Parallel\u252 \'fcberlieferung: Wien, Erzbisch\u246 \'f6fl. Di\u246 \'f6zesanA, Kirnberger B der Wiener Dompropstei, Cod. B-8, 141\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf1 . \endash  (Nr. 8) Mit gleichem Wortlaut \u252 \'fcberliefert in: Manuale Henrici Sistaricensis episcopi (Henricus de Segusio, 1200-1270), in: \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf17 Thesaurus novus anecdotorum 4, ed. Edmond \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf17 Mart\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf17 \u232 \'e8\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf17 ne\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf17  / Ursin \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf17 Durand\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf17 . ND Farnborough/Hampshire 1969, Sp. 1079-1098, hier Sp. 1093 Nr. LXXXII. \endash  (Nr. 10bc) Monumenta Tachygraphica Codicis Parisiensis Latini 2718. Fasc. alter: Sancti Iohannis Chrysostomi libros II Latine versos continens, ed. Wilhelm \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf17 Schmitz\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf17 . Hannover 1883. \endash  (Nr. 11) Bonaventura, Sermones de tempore, Dominica infra octavam epiphaniae, sermo 3, in: Bonaventura, Opera omnia 13, ed. Adolphe Charles \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf17 Peltier\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf17 . Paris 1868, Sp. 82a Z. 33-37.}

