\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf17 221\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf17 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf17  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf17 Figurae astronomicae
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa120\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 \u220 \'dcberschrift auf 221\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  unten, auf 221\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  oben wiederholt, mit roter Tinte \u252 \'fcbermalt: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 DE ASTROLOGIA\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 . \endash  Sieben Diagramme, Umrisslinien rot, Beschriftung schwarz; Sigle der Hs. nach \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Eastwood\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 /\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Gra\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ss\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 hoff\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , S. 152: Cap24. \endash  Diagramm 1 (1. Reihe): \u8218 \'82Equales-Inequales\lquote  nach lib. 8 \u167 \'a7 844 (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Eastwood\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 /\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Gra\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ss\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 hoff\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , S. 123f.; Ed. S. 444 Z. 1-5). \endash  Diagramm 2 (2. Reihe links): \u8218 \'82Three versions\lquote  nach lib. 8 \u167 \'a7 857 (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Eastwood\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 /\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Gra\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ss\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 hoff\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , S. 129f.; Ed. S. 450 Z. 19-S. 451 Z. 4). \endash  Diagramm 3 (2. Reihe rechts oben): \u8218 \'82Eclipsis\lquote  nach lib. 8 \u167 \'a7 869 (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Eastwood\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 /\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Gra\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ss\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 hoff\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , S. 127-129; Ed. S. 457 Z. 21-S. 459 Z. 4). \endash  Diagramm 4 (2. Reihe rechts Mitte) \u8218 \'82Libra-Aries\lquote  nach lib. 8 \u167 \'a7 872 (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Eastwood\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 /\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Gra\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ss\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 hoff\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , S. 117-119; Ed. S. 460 Z. 5-11). \endash  Diagramm 5 (2. Reihe unten): \u8218 \'82Condicione partium\lquote  nach lib. 8 \u167 \'a7 880 (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Eastwood\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 /\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Gra\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ss\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 hoff\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , S. 119f.; Ed. S. 464 Z. 15-17). \endash  Diagramm 6 (3. Reihe rechts): \u8218 \'82Ultra triginta\lquote  nach lib. 8 \u167 \'a7 880 (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Eastwood\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 /\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Gra\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ss\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 hoff\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , S. 125f.; Ed. 464 Z. 9-12). \endash  Diagramm 7 (3. Reihe links): \u8218 \'82Equinoctium\lquote  nach lib. 8 \u167 \'a7 878 (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Eastwood\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 /\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Gra\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ss\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 hoff\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 , S. 124f.; Ed. S. 463 Z. 10-17).
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf18 Abb.: Bruce Stansfield \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\cf18 Eastwood\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf18  / Gerd \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\cf18 Gra\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\cf18 ss\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\cf18 hoff\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf18 , Planetary Diagrams for Roman Astronomy in Medieval Europe ca. 800-1500. Philadelphia 2004 (Transactions of the American Philosophical Society 94,3). \endash  Lit.: Bruce Stansfield \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\cf18 Eastwood\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf18 , Plato and Circumsolar Planetary Motion in the Middle Ages, in: Archives d'histoire doctrinale et litt\u233 \'e9raire du Moyen \u194 \'c2ge 68 (1993), S. 7-26, Hs. genannt S. 15 Anm. 27; Mariken \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\cf18 Teeuwen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf18 , \u8218 \'82The Master Has it Wrong\lquote . Dissenting Voices in Commentary Texts, in: Auctor et auctoritas in latinis medii aevi litteris = Author and Authorship in Medieval Latin Literature. Proceedings of the VIth Congress of the International Medieval Latin Committee (Benevento-Naples, November 9-13, 2010), ed. Edoardo \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\cf18 D'Angelo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf18  / Jan \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\cf18 Ziolkowski\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf18 . Florenz 2014 (MediEVI 4), S. 1097-1108, hier S. 1104 und Anm. 20 (Hs. genannt).}

