\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 (39\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 -41\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ) \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Chalcidius, Commentarium in Timaeum Platonis (Ausz\u252 \'fcge)
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 pars 2, cap. 283-295 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Nihil eorum que sunt generatum esse nec periturum fore \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 (40\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 non numquam pro portione.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (41\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ) cap. 299 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Deus itaque siluam magnifica uirtute comebat \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 piaculo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 . (Z. 11) cap. 303-304: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Sunt uicina nobis omnia quidem que sentiuntur .ignis.aer.aqua. \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 exemplaris origo rerum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 .
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Ed. Plato Latinus IV. Timaeus. A Calcidio translatus commentarioque instructus, ed. Jan Hendrik \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Waszink\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . London/Leiden 1962 (Corpus Platonicum medii aevi), S. 286,9-295,10; 301,4-13, 304,18-306,8. Diese Hs. in der Liste der Manuskripte nicht verzeichnet. \endash  Weitere kurze Exzerpte s.u. 48\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , 51\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 rv\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 .}

