\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa120\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 68\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 -70\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Isidorus Hispalensis: Etymologiarum sive Originum libri XX\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (lib. 7, cap. 6, versio abbreviata)
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa120\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 DE HOMINIBUS QUI QUODAM PRAESAGIO NOMINA ACCEPERUNT\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Adam sicut beatus Hieronimus tradidit homo seu terrenus siue terra rubra interpretatur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 in Babilone enim ortus est. Ibi et princeps\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  [gentis Iudaeae] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 extitit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (PL 82, 274-281B). Von anderer Hand: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Ananehel gratissimus dei\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (vgl. Rupertus Tuitensis, In Zachariam prophetam commentariorum lib. 5, PL 168, 809B).
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 CPL 1186; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Stegm\u252 \'fcller, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 RB 3 (9,1) Nr. 5164; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 D\u237 \'edaz y D\u237 \'edaz\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Index, S. 39-41 Nr. 122 (ohne diese Hs.).}

