\pard\fi0\li0\qc\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 III (Bl. 44-159)
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 44\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 -159\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Marcus Annaeus Lucanus: Pharsalia. Cum glossis interlinearibus et marginalibus latinis et germanicis
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 44\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  bis auf wenige verblasste Federproben leer. \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 Incipit LVCANVS\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \u8249 \'8b\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  Lib. 1: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 BELLA per Emathios plus quam ciuilia campos\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 hec ait, et lasso iacuit deserta furore\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 . \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\caps\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 Explicit Lvcani liber primus. Incipit secvndvs\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \u8249 \'8b. \endash  (54\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 ) Lib. 2; \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 (65\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ) lib. 3; (75\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ) lib. 4; (87\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ) lib. 5; (99\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ) lib. 6; (111\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ) lib. 7; (123\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ) lib. 8; (136\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ) lib. 9; (151\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ) lib. 10: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Ut primum terras Pompei colla secutus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 obsedit muris calcantem menia magnvm\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 . \endash  (159\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ) Besitzvermerk von anderer, wohl zeitgen\u246 \'f6ssischer Hand: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Iste liber pertinet ad sanctum \plain \f1\i\caps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Emmeramum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (derselbe Eintrag in verblasster Schrift in vorhergehender Zeile). \endash  B\u252 \'fccherfluch (3 Verse): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Non videat Christum, qui librvm subtrahit \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 (Sanftl: subtrahat) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 istvm\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  | \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Qui me furetur, perpes sibi pena paretu\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r | \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Furtepotens\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (!, furto potens?) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 librvm, si quis sibi vendicet istvm\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Sanftl\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  III, p. 1665).
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Edition: M. Annaei Lucani De bello civili. Libri X = Pharsalia, ed. David R. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Shackleton Bailey\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Berlin u.a. 2009 (Bibliotheca scriptorum Graecorum et Romanorum Teubneriana 1502). \endash  Lit.: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Munk Olsen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , L\rquote \u233 \'e9tude 2, S. 51 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 [C. 99]\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 ; Bd. 3,1, S. 198. \endash  Emmeramer Parallel\u252 \'fcberlieferung des B\u252 \'fccherfluchs: Clm 14124, 153\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  (v. 2); 14160, 1a\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  (v. 2).}

