\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Fortlaufender Kommentartext: Prolog, Satura 1,1-35 (\u8222 \'84gemischte\ldblquote  Fassung)
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 (162\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  Z. 1) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Unde Martianus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Et fons Gorgonei tulit caballi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 quia in laudem uirtutis eam uictricem prosiliunt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (Ed.: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Jahn\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 , S. 241 Z. 32-S. 242 Z. 7; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Zetzel\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 , App. III Adn. 1e, S. 195 Z. 15-23; Trad. E, S. 306 Pr. 1 \u167 \'a7 6-9; Trad. B, kop (m)/vos (m) ad 0.1). \endash  (Z. 9) \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \u8218 \'82\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Nec in bicipiti\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \u8230 \'85\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \lquote \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (Pr. 2). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Parnason Delforum montem dicit, qui habet duo cacumina, Nason Libero sacrum, Cirram Apollini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 quod eius anima in suo corpore esset\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (Ed.: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Jahn\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 , S. 245 \u167 \'a7 2; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Clausen/Zetzel\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 , S. 2 \u167 \'a7 2.1-3; Trad. A, S. 7 \u167 \'a7 2.1-3; Trad. E, S. 306f. \u167 \'a7 2.1-2; Trad. B, vos (m), ad 0.2). \endash  (Z. 15) \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \u8218 \'82\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Quis expediuit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \u8230 \'85\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \lquote \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (Pr. 8). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Hoc dicit, quod \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 non\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  (\u252 \'fcbergeschrieben)\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 omnes natura sunt poete\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 [ut] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 naturaliter uideatur loqui, qui esurit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  (Ed.: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Clausen/Zetzel\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 , S. 3 \u167 \'a7 8.1-3; Trad. A, S. 8 \u167 \'a7 8.1-3; Trad. E, S. 307f. \u167 \'a7 8.2-4; vgl. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Jahn\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 , S. 246f. \u167 \'a7 8). \endash  (Z. 19) \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \u8218 \'82\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 Coruos poetas\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  \u8230 \'85\lquote  (Pr. 13)\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 quod coruino lucro inducti non solum cantare\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 [\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 possint\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 ],\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 sed etiam carmen fingere\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (vgl. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Jahn\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 , S. 247 \u167 \'a7 13; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Clausen/Zetzel\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 , S. 3 \u167 \'a7 13; Trad. A, S. 8 \u167 \'a7 13.1; Trad. E, S. 308 \u167 \'a7 13.1; Trad. B, kop (m)/vos (m) ad 0.13). \endash  (Z. 22) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Genus humanum plenum est curis et sollicitudinibus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 qui etiam de diuinis rebus tractare uoluerunt et exponunt, quantum est in ipsis inquit tracta\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 [\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ti\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 ]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 onibus inane ridendum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (Ed.: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Zetzel\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 , App. III Sat. 1.1 b-d, S. 197 Z. 15-20 mit Textzusatz aus Variantenapparat; vgl. auch Trad. E, S. 309 \u167 \'a7 1.2-4; Trad. B, vos (m) ad. 1.1). \endash  (Z. 28) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Ait ergo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \u8218 \'82\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Curas hominum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \lquote  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 inanes,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1  quia sine fructu laborare uelint\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 (Ed.: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Clausen/Zetzel\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 , S. 4 \u167 \'a7 1.2; Trad. A, S. 10 \u167 \'a7 1.4; Trad. B, kop (m)/vos (m) ad. 1.1). \endash  (Z. 29) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Uidens Persius multos libidinari in scribendo ad hoc tantum, ut fauorem populi acquirerent, reprehendendo cum indignatione inchoat ex abrupto. Nam ante phylosophye stu\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ||\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 [\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 duit apud Bassum primo, deinde apud Cornutum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 ]\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (Ed.: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Zetzel\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 , App. III Sat. 1.1 a, S. 197 Z. 12-14; Trad. B, kop (m)/vos (m) ad. 1.0). \endash  (Z. 32) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Semetipsum arguit, quod relinquat carmina, que uulgus lecturum non sit, quoniam non sunt uulgaria, quia minime conueniat libidini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (Ed.: Trad. A, S. 10 \u167 \'a7 1.1; Trad. B, kop (m)/vos (m) ad. 1.2; vgl. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Clausen/Zetzel\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 , S. 4 \u167 \'a7 1.1).
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 (162\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  Z. 1) \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \u8218 \'82\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 Labeonem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \lquote  (Sat. 1,4). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 Labeonis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 recitator Pollidama. Labeo poeta latinus fuit, qui \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 [carmen]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  et opus Homeri conuertit in latinum sermonem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  ego de moribus et propria cudo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  (\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Ed.: \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 Trad. E, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 S. 309 \u167 \'a7 4/7.1-2); (Z. 5) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 eius autem uerivs\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (!, recte versus) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 est\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Crudum manduces Priamum Priamo pisingos\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (Ed.: Trad. A, S. 11 \u167 \'a7 4.5). \endash  (Z. 6) \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \u8218 \'82\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 Tun, uetule\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \lquote  (Sat. 1,22), \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 id est stulte, qui sinescis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  (!, recte senescis) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 in uilibvs carminibus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f2\i\lang1024\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 eius etatis homo uan\u281 \'ea glorie esse captator\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  (\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Ed.: Trad. A, S. 19 \u167 \'a7 22.2-3); (Z. 8) \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \u8218 \'82\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 Escas\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \lquote \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 autem dicit fauorem, id est delectationem vel concilias ex fauore imperitorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (ebd. \u167 \'a7 22. 5). \endash  (Z. 9) \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \u8218 \'82\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Auriculis quibus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \lquote \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (Sat. 1,23) \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 [id est] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 inperitis et spurcissimis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 etiam in cute\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  [possis] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 habere\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (ebd. S. 20 \u167 \'a7 23.1-4); (Z. 11) \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \u8218 \'82\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 Ohe\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \lquote  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 interiectio cum admiratione percontantis est etiam uox exultantis, vnde Iuuenalis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 Satur est cum dicit Orativs ohe\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 (Ed.: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Z\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 etzel\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 , App. III Sat. 1.23 d, S. 200 Z. 26f.). \endash  (Z. 13) \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \u8218 \'82\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 Ten cirratorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \lquote  (Sat. 1,29). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 Sic Persivs dicit: Cur non debes letari. Ceretis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  (!, recte Certe) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 maxima est gloria laudari\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  [a] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 c\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 [entum] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 cirrat\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 [is] (\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Ed.: \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 Trad. A, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 S. 22 \u167 \'a7 29.2); (Z. 15) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Cirrati sunt scolastici. Cirri enim dicuntur capilli, et illi crines habebant in honore Ueneris, quos statuto tempore metebant\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (Ed.: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Z\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 etzel\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 , App. III Sat. 1.29 d, S. 201 Z. 19f.; vgl. auch Trad. B, kop (m)/vos (m) ad 1.29); (Z. 16) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Intantum est scientia tua ad nihilum deducta, ut aliquid te scire nescias, nisi alterivs iudicium de scientia tua consulas\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (Ed.: Trad. A, S. 21 \u167 \'a7 26/27.3). \endash  (Z. 19) \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \u8218 \'82\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 R\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ancidulum quiddam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \lquote  (Sat. 1,33) [id est]\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 putridum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (vgl. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 Trad. E, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 S. 315 \u167 \'a7 33.1). \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \u8218 \'82\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Phillisdas\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \lquote \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (!, recte Phyllidas) (Sat. 1,34). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Phillis regina fuit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 [\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 T\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 ]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 racum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8230 \'85 ad eius nuptias reuersurum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (Ed.: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Z\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 etzel\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 , App. III Sat. 1.34 a, S. 201 Z. 31-34); (Z. 23) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Profectusque est, et cum tardaret, Phillis amoris impatientia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 unde etiam Phillida\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (!, recte Philla) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 dicta s\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 unt a Phillide\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  (\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Ed.: \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 Trad. E, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 S. 315 \u167 \'a7 34.2-3); (Z. 28) \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \u8218 \'82\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 Isyphilas\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \lquote  (!, recte \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Hypsipylas) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 una ex Lemnadibus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 [mulieribus] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 fuit, Liberi patris neptis, Thoantis filia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 ut audientivm aures emoliant\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 (ebd. \u167 \'a7 34.4-5, mit Abweichungen; vgl. auch Trad. A, S. 23f. \u167 \'a7 34.3-4). \endash  (Z. 32) \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \u8218 \'82\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Tenero\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \lquote \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (Sat.1, 35) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 id est molli et fragili\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ; \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \u8218 \'82\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Subplantat\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 \lquote \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 [id est]\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 uocis canora mutantis accentibus curtant, quasi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 [sonus] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1 uocis canore\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8\cf1  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 (Ed.: Trad. A, S. 24 \u167 \'a7 35.2-3; vgl. auch Trad. D, S. 175 \u167 \'a7 35.2-3).
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb240\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Der Kommentar, den das eingef\u252 \'fcgte, m\u246 \'f6glicherweise aus einer anderen Hs. stammende Bl. 162 \u252 \'fcberliefert, l\u228 \'e4sst sich nicht eindeutig einem bestimmten \u220 \'dcberlieferungszweig der Vulgattradition zuweisen; vielmehr scheint es sich hier um eine Mischung aus den Traditionen A, B und E zu handeln (\u8222 \'84gemischte\ldblquote  Fassung). M\u246 \'f6glicherweise lagen dem Kompilator mehrere Hss. vor, aus denen er das Kommentargut frei kombinieren konnte. Dieses Vorgehen entspricht der bei \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Scholz/Wiener\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , S. XXV, mitgeteilten Beobachtung, das die ohnehin nicht eindeutig abgrenzbaren Vulgattraditionen trotz \u8222 \'84einer gewissen Textkonstanz\ldblquote  Kommentargut aus unterschiedlichen Bearbeitungen aufweisen, weshalb sie oftmals \u8222 \'84an den R\u228 \'e4ndern \u8230 \'85 flie\u223 \'dfend und fransig\ldblquote  sind. \endash  Abk\u252 \'fcrzungen: Pr. = Prolog; Sat. = Satura; Trad. = Tradition. \endash  Editionen: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Jahn\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  und \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Clausen/Zetzel\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  s. vorheriger Abschnitt. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Zetzel\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  = James E. G. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Zetzel\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Marginal Scholarship and Textual Deviance. The \u8218 \'82Commentum Cornuti\lquote  and the Early Scholia on Persius. London 2005 (Bulletin of the Institute of Classical Studies. Supplement 84), Appendix III, S. 193-227. \endash  Trad. A = Persius-Scholien. Die lateinische Persius-Kommentierung der Traditionen A, D und E, eingeleitet und hrsg. von Udo W. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Scholz\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  / Claudia \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Wiener\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Wiesbaden 2009 (Wissensliteratur im Mittelalter 46), S. 2-152. \endash  Trad. D = ebd. S. 153-301. \endash  Trad. E = ebd. S. 302-367. \endash  Trad. B = Glossae in Persium. Die Persius-Glossen der sogenannten Tradition B, hrsg. von Martin \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Hellmann\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  / Stefan \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Ullrich\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  / Claudia \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Wiener\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Editing glosses (LMUexcellent) 2010 (online-Ressource: http://www.persius.mueze.uni-muenchen.de/ghtm/gfr.htm); herangezogen wurden die Textzeugen: kop (m) = Kopenhagen, KB, Gl. Kgl. S. 2028 4\u176 \'b0, 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 -24\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 ; vos (m) = Leiden, UB, Voss. lat. Q 18, 69\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 -90\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . \endash  Lit.: Dorothy M. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Robathan\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  / F. Edward \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Cranz\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  with the assistance of Paul Oskar \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Kristeller\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  and with a contribution by Bernhard \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Bischoff\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , A. Persius Flaccus, in: Catalogus translationum et commentariorum. Mediaeval and Renaissance Latin Translations and Commentaries. Annoted Lists and Guides. Bd. 2, ed. Paul Oskar \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Kristeller\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  / F. Edward \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Cranz\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Washington 1976, S. 201-312, zur sog. Vulgattradition S. 212-237; Paola \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Scarcia Piacentini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Saggio di un censimento dei manoscritti contenenti il testo di Persio e gli scoli e i commenti al testo. Rom 1973 (Studi sulla tradizione di Persio e la scoliastica persiana. Serie 2; Studio su Persio e la scoliastica persiana 3,1), S. 5-125, hier S. 62 Nr. 291; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Munk Olsen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , L\rquote \u233 \'e9tude 2, S. 201 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 [C. 47]\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 ; Bd. 3,2, S. 107 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 [C. 47]\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 .}

