\pard\fi0\li0\qc\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 II (Bl. 27-70)
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 27\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 -43\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Thomas Cisterciensis: In Cantica canticorum commentarii (lib. 7-12)
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Quilibet homo tres habet sorores. Prima corruptionis temptatio, secunda ratio, tertia sapientie persulto \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (!) \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 et Lazarus unus est ex recumbentibus, quem pascit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (lib. 7 ad Ct 5,1, PL 206, 486CD). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (Z. 10) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Uinum tria facit: calefacit, letificat et inebriat. Sic et spiritus sanctus calefacit adueniendo, letificat uisitando, inebriat se habvndantius fundendo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 per uinum intelligitur sanguis, nam ex uino conficitur. Vnde dicitur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Lauit nos a peccatis n\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ostris\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ]\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 a sa\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [nguine] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 s\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [uo] (Apc 1,5)\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (lib. 7 ad Ct 5,1, ebd. 488D-489B)\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 3\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 (Z. 23) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Nox est quamdiu homo in peccato est. Hec nox quatuor habet uigilias\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 hoc est quando delectationes mundi libenter aspicivnt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (lib. 7 ad Ct 5,2, ebd. 502AC). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (27\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Z. 7-18) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Triplex est siccitas\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 contritio sine lacrimis, sine misericordia compassio, sine deuotione contemplatio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 de primo dicitur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Rorate, c\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 eli\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ]\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 d\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 esuper\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ]\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 (Is 45,8). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 De secundo Osee propheta\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Ero quasi ros\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 (Os 14,6) (lib. 7 ad Ct 5,2, ebd. 516C-517A) \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 5\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (41\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Z. 7-43\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Z. 28) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Fuge, dilecte mi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Ct 8,14). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Hic sermo et de triumpho dominice ascensionis et de his, que in ecclesia sancta cottidie geruntur, recte potest accipi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 iam eam osculatur os\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [culo] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 oris sui, id est eius presentia delectatur, qua perpetuo fruitur, sponso prestante, qui cum patre\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 A M E N\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (lib. 12 ad Ct 8,14, ebd. 847D-860D). \endash  Nachtr\u228 \'e4ge: \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 6\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (43\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Z. 28-36) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Sunt canales, in quibus adhuc rudis purpura tingitur, sunt in quibus obscurata lauantur, sunt in quibus inueterata renouantur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 audi Paulum renouantem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 :\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Si enim sanguis hir\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 corum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ]\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ad emu\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ndationem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ]\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 car\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 nis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ]\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Hbr 9,13) (lib. 10, ad Ct 7,4f., ebd. 724B). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 7\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (Z. 36-43\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Z. 28) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Quatuor sunt porte\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 :\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  prima ad orientem, secunda ad austrum, tertia ad aquilonem, quarta ad orientem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 in quarta dum ad celum erigunt sua desideria, vnde\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Sitiuit anima\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 m\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ea\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ]\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ad deum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Ps 41,3) (lib. 11 ad Ct 7,13, ebd. 753C-755B).
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1 Exzerpte aus dem Hohenlied-Kommentar des Thomas von Perseigne. Lediglich Beginn (Nr. 1-4) und Schluss (Nr. 5-7) werden aufgef\u252 \'fchrt. \endash  Druck: PL 206, 21-860. \endash  Zum Verfasser s. Maur \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\cf1 Standaert\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1 , Art. Thomas le Cistercien, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf1 in: \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1 DSAM 15 (1991) Sp. 796-800 (mit weiterf\u252 \'fchrender Lit.); Marc-Ailko \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\cf1 Aris\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1 , Art. Thomas de Perseigne, in: LexMA 8 (1997), Sp. 722\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8\cf1 .}

