\pard\fi0\li0\qc\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 II (Bl. 141-195)
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 141\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 -156\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Coniugatio verborum
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 INCIPIUNT CONIUGATIONES VERBORUM. INCIPT PRIMA CONIUGATIO\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 \u8249 \'8b \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 AMO UERBVM ACTIUVM\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [IN] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 INDICAtiuo modo dictum, temporis presentis, numeri singularis, figure simplicis, person\plain \f2\i\lang1024\fs24 \u281 \'ea\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  prim\plain \f2\i\lang1024\fs24 \u281 \'ea\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 , quod coniugabitur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (korr. aus declinabitur) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 sic\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Amo, amas, amat et pluraliter\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 amamus, amatis, amant. Eodem modo tempore preterito imperfecto\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Amabam, amabis, amabat, et pluraliter\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 amabamus, amabatis, amabant\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85; (143\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) secunda coniugatio; (144\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) tertia coniugatio; (146\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) quarta coniugatio; (148\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) verba anomala: esse; (149\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) velle; (150\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) edere; (151\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) ire; (151\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) ferre; (153\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) fieri; (153\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) gaudere; (154\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) mereri; (155\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) mederi; (155\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) noscere; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ODI, ODISTI, ODIT. ET \plain \f1\i\caps\lang1033\fs24 pluraliter\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ODIMUS, ODISTIS, oderunt vel re\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Alia duo uerba sunt, id est memini et c\plain \f2\i\lang1024\fs24 \u281 \'eapi, de quibus nulla dubitatio est, quod secundum regulam tantum preterita declinantur, nisi in\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 peratiuo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Lit.: Geoffrey L. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Bursill-Hall\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , A Check-list of Incipits of Medieval Latin Grammatical Treatises, in: Traditio 34 (1978), S. 439-474, hier S. 448; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Bursill-Hall, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 S. 154 Nr. 176.144.1 (jeweils diese Hs. genannt).}

