\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 194\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Paulus Camaldulensis: Donatus (Exz.)
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Amo requirit imperatiuo modo tempore presenti ametur, futuro ametur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!, recte amator). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Optatiuo modo tempore presenti et preterito inperfecto utinam amaretur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 infinitiuo modo tempore presenti amari, preterito amatum esse vel amatum fuisse, futuro amatum iri\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Ed. S. 139 Z. 34-44). \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Doceo requirit imperatiuo modo tempore presenti doceatur, futuro doceatur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!, recte docetor). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Optatiuo modo tempore presenti utinam doceretur, preterito plusquamperfecto utinam doctum esset vel doctum fuisset, futuro utinam doceatur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 infinitiuo modo numeris et personis doceri, preterito doctum esse vel doctum fuisse, futuro doctum iri\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Ed. S. 140 Z. 9-S. 142 Z. 88).
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 Edition: Il Donatus di Paolo Camaldolese, ed. critica a cura di Vito \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 Sivo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 . Spoleto 1990 (Testi, studi, strumenti 2). \endash  Lit.: \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Michael \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Boutroix\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Paul the Camaldolite's Prologue and Grammatical Treatise, in: Manuscripta 16 (1972), S. 169-174, hier S. 169, 171, 173 (diese Hs. jeweils genannt).}

