\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 208\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 -225\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Ars Ambianensis: Declinationes nominum (Redactio \plain \f1\b\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 MOW\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 )
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\i\caps\lang1033\fs24 Incipiunt quinque Declinationes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Omnia nomina, quibus Latina utitur eloquentia, quinque declinationibus flectuntur, quae ordinem acceperunt ab ordine uocalium formantium genitiuos\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 in ceteris uero casibus regulam nominis sequuntur in ultimis syllabis, vt Honoratus dicit: Reliqui quoque casus regulam sumunt ex nomine\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Edition (u.a. nach dieser Hs.): Ars Ambianensis. Le tre redazioni delle \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 \u8218 \'82\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 declinationes nominum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 \lquote \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , a cura di Claudio \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Giammona\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Hildesheim 2016 (Bibliotheca Weidmanniana 6; Collectanea grammatica Latina 14), S. 83-112, zu dieser Hs. s. S. XLII-XLIV, mit Sigle \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs20 M\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  bezeichnet. \endash  Lit.: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Jeudy\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , L'Institutio (s.o. 188\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 ), S. 83f., laut der es sich bei diesem Traktat um eine Bearbeitung von Priscians Institutio de nomine, pronomine et verbo durch Walahfrid Strabo handelt; Vivian \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Law\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , The Transmission of Early Medieval Elementary Grammars. A Case Study in Explanation, in: Formative Stages of Classical Traditions. Latin Texts from Antiquity to the Renaissance. Proceedings of a Conference held at Erice, 16-22 October 1993, ed. by Oronzo \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Pecere\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  / Michael D. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Reeve\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Spoleto 1995 (Biblioteca del Centro per il Collegamento degli Studi Medievali e Umanistici in Umbria 15), S. 239-261, hier S. 243-245, 250-252 (diese Hs. genannt S. 244 und S. 252 Anm. 13)\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 ;\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  James E.G. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Zetzel\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Critics, Compilers, and Commentators. An Introduction to Roman Philology, 200 BCE-800 CE. New York 2018, S. 357.}

