\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 69\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 -70\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Sermo in Mt 15,28
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 Quadragesima. \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 16\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 In illo tempore egressus Ihesus secessit in partes Tiri et Sidonis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Mt 15,28). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Hoc ewangelium scribitur Mathei 15 capitulo et legitur dominica secunda in Quadragesima, in quo Christus ostendit nobis procurationem filie mulieris Chananee, vt nos exemplo suo, si non statim in principio exaudiamus propter hoc ab inpetracione incepta non cessemus, sed feruencius inpetrando insistemus. Et diuititur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 in quattuor partes, secundum quod fides huius mulieris Chananee ex quattuor commendatur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  (69\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Ex ewangelio inni\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [ti]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 tur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (?) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 questio, quare Christus tantam duritiam ostendit, cum ipse sit summe misericors\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 vnde sanctus apostolus dicit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Sancti per fidem vicerunt regna, operati sunt iusticiam, adepti \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [re]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 promissiones\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Hbr 11,33). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Sicut mulier Cha\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [na]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 nea. Sicut Abraham\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Dy heyligen, dy haben durch den gelauben\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  70\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  leer.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 71\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 -76\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Sermo in Mt 4,2
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 Quadragesima. \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 17\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Et cum ieiunasset quadraginta diebus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Mt 4,2). \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 a\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Pro introductione sciendum, quod Haymo scribit super predicta uerba sic dicens\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 In huius lectionis serie vtramque suam naturam, diuinam scilicet et humanam, nobis dominus manifestare dignatus est\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  (Z. 10) \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 sed quasi deus temptationes superavit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 b\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (71\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Item ieiunium est triplex\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 primum corporis a cibo materiali\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (korr. aus temporali), \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 secundum afflictionis a gaudio temporali\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  Rest der Seite sowie 72\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  leer. \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 c\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (72\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) De multiplici effectu ieiunii: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Primo dei misericordiam impetrat. Exemplum habemus in Niniuitis Ione iii, que facto ieiunio, misericordiam dei obtinuerunt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (vgl. Ion 3,10). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Secundo ad diuinorum integritatem et veram sapientiam hominem disponit. Dan 10\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Tollebat Manassar\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!, recte Malasar) \u8230 \'85 (Dn 1,16) \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 decimo aduersitates depellit temporales. I Esdre 8\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Ieiunauimus et rogamus dominum et euenit nobis prospere\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (I Esr 8,23). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 d\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (73\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Ieiunium in peccato mortali factum non prodest ad uitam eternam. Prodest tamen ad tria\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Primum est obseruatio mandati uel impletio, ad quod tenebatur \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 hec Albertus in li\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [bro] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 de iiii\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [sententiarum] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 co\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [mmentario]\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 eius\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  in tractatu de iiii vir\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [tutibus] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 car\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [dinalibus] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 di. 63\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 e\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 (73\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Jeiunium quattuor commutari dicunt secundum Raymundum. Item largitas, vnde Jeronimus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Quid manducaturus erat, si non ieiunares, da pauperibus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 virtus, id est virtuosus, ut mereatur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 f\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 (74\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Quidam frater interrogabat abbatem Macharium, cur fame ab hora tercia pulsaretur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 et cenodoxie refectio sagniauit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (!, recte saginavit). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Hec in collectione Serapionis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 . \endash  Rest der Seite leer. \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 g\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (74\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Item a ieiunio duo sunt, que excusant, scilicet etas et necessitas. Primo a ieiunio absoluit et excusat etas, propter quam pueri a ieiunio absoluuntur, et hoc propter duas causas. Prima propter nature debilitatem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 sicut etiam de iumentis legitur Ione III\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Homines et iumenta non gustent quidquam, nec bibant aquam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Ion 3,7) (Sum. theol. II\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 a\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -IIae, qu. 147 art. 4 ad 2). \endash  (Z. 20) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Secundo absoluit a ieiunio necessitas, propter quam absoluuntur infirmi et debiles, pauperes mendicantes, peregrinantes, operarii, pregnantes, lactantes, cursores et seruitores\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  (Z. 23) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Primo infirmi et debiles\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 (Sum. conf., lib. 1 tit. 12 qu. 25, Bl. xxxv\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ); (75\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Z. 7) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Secundo a ieiunio absoluuntur pauperes mendicantes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 (Sent., lib. 4 dist. 15 qu. 3 art. 2 qc. 4 ad 2; Sum. theol. II\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 a\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -IIae, qu. 147 art. 4 ad 4); (Z. 19) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Tercio peregrinantes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 (Sent., lib. 4 dist. 15 qu. 3 art. 2 qc. 4 ad 1; Sum. theol. II\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 a\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -IIae, qu. 147 art. 4 ad 3); (75\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Z. 10) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Quarto operarii siue laboratores agrorum, vinearum et huiusmodi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 (Sent., lib. 4 dist. 15 qu. 3 art. 2 qc. 4 ad 3). \endash  (76\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Quinto mulieres pregnantes et nutrices\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 (Sum. conf., lib. 1 tit. 12 qu. 24, Bl. xxxv\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ). \endash  Rest der Seite frei.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Zitatbelege: (a) Haimo Altissiodorensis, Homiliae de tempore, hom. 28, PL 118,190C. \endash  (b) Lemma Jeiunium, in: Die Vokabulare von Fritsche Closener und Jakob Twinger von K\u246 \'f6nigshofen. Bd. 1: Einleitung. Text A-Im, hrsg. von Klaus \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Kirchert\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , bearb. von Dorothea \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Klein\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . T\u252 \'fcbingen 1995 (Texte und Textgeschichte 40), S. 705. \endash  (c) Guillelmus Peraldus, Summa vitiorum, tract. 5 De iustitia, pars 11, cap. 6, in: Guilielmi Peraldi \u8230 \'85 Summae virtutum ac vitiorum tomus I et II. Hac postrema editione \u8230 \'85 studio et opera Rodolphi \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Clutii\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . K\u246 \'f6ln 1614 (VD17 12:135421H), Bd. 1, S. 291 Z. 4-S. 292 Z. 2. \endash  (d) Rainerus de Pisia, Pantheologia, sub lemmate Ieiunium, cap. 7, verglichen mit GW M36944 = BSB-Ink R-6, Bl. 256\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  Z. 7-18; vgl. auch Die \u8222 \'84Rechtssumme\ldblquote  Bruder Bertholds. Eine deutsche abecedarische Bearbeitung der \u8222 \'84Summa Confessorum\ldblquote  des Johannes von Freiburg. Synoptische Edition der Fassungen B, A und C. Bd. 6: Quellenkommentar, Buchstabenbereich A-H, hrsg. von Georg \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Steer\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  / Marlies \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Hamm\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . T\u252 \'fcbingen 1991 (Texte und Textgeschichte 16), S. 300. \endash  Das von Rainerus angef\u252 \'fchrte Albert-Zitat stammt aus: Sancti \u8230 \'85 Alberti Magni \u8230 \'85 Opera omnia. Bd. 28: De bono, primum ediderunt Henricus \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 K\u252 \'fchle\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  / Carolus \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Feckes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  / Bernardus \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Geyer\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  / Wilhelmus \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 K\u252 \'fcbel\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . M\u252 \'fcnster 1951, tract. 3 De temperantia, qu. 2 De continentia, art. 6 De observantia ieiuniorum Nr. 251, S. 146. \endash  (e) Druck: Albericus de Rosate, Dictionarium Iuris Utriusque. Venedig 1572, Bl. X\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 [\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 7\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 ]\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  Z. 34-46\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 . \endash  (f) \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Thomas de Hibernia: Manipulus florum; Edition: https://manipulus-project.wlu.ca/index.html, sub lemmate: Ieiunium ak; Druck: u.a. VD16 T 1090, S. 445. \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 (g)\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  Gew\u228 \'e4hrung von Fastendispensen auf der Grundlage von: 1. Sum. theol. = Thomas de Aquino, Summa theologiae, II\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 a\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 -IIae, qu. 147 art. 4; 2. Sent. = Thomas de Aquino, Scriptum super Sententiis, lib. 4 dist. 15 qu. 3 art. 2 qc. 4; 3. Sum. conf. = Johannes de Friburgo, Summa confessorum, lib. 1 tit. 12. Druck: Paris: Jean Petit, 1519. Vgl. auch Albericus de Rosate (s.o. e), Bl. X\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 [\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 7\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 ]\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 va\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 .}

