\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 189\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 -197\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Conradus de Brundelsheim: Sermones de pace
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 Octava Paschae. \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 43\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 In der Kopfzeile: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 In octaua pasce sermo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 a\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Pax vobis \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (Io 20,19; 20,21; 20,26) \u8230 \'85 (nicht lesbar wegen Wasserschaden). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Augustinus in sermone de pace\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Tantum est pacis donum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!, recte bonum), \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ut et in rebus creatis atque moralibus nihil gracius solebat\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (korr. zu \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 solet\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , recte soleat) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 audiri, nihil desiderabilius concupisci, nihil melius possit inveniri\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 tercius in premio futurorum, quid est eterna gloria\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 b\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (194\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Z. 17) Guilelmus Peraldus: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Nota, quod multa sunt, que ad pacem habendam valere possunt. Primo est amor pacis. Romanorum 14\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Que pacis sunt, sectamur inuicem et in omnes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (vgl. Rm 14,19). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Secundum est mutacio peccati, quia prouerbiorun 16 dicitur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Conplacuerint\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!, recte Cum placuerint) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 domino vie eius\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Prv 16,7) \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 decimum est oratio. Iob 18\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Si diluculo consurrexeris ad deum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Iob 8,5-5). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Vltimum est custodia sensuum, vnde eciam ianuis clausis dictum est a domino discipulis suis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Pax vobis. Johannis 20\u176 \'b0\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (vgl. Io 20,26). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 c\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (195\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Z. 5) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 De tercio pace exhibita siue precepta cum bonis et malis hominibus. Primo pax trepida\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (?, turbida?) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 cum malis hominibus est cum ipsorum lesiones, inpugnaciones, inquietaciones, tribulaciones, detractiones siue retribuciones mali cordis et oris et operis pacifice tolleramus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 hanc pacem optabat nobis apostolus primo ad The\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [ssalonicenses] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 iii\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Deus pacis \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 det nobis pacem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (II Th 3,16). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Ideo eciam eodem 22\u176 \'b0\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Deus pacis sanctificet nos per omnia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (I Th 5,23).
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Zitatbelege: (a) Conradus de Brundelsheim, Sermones de tempore (Sermones Socci), pars aestivalis, sermo 10: Dominica in octava Paschae; Druck: GW 7410 = BSB-Ink C-520, Bl. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 [B5]\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 va\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 -[B6]\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 . \endash  (b) Druck: \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Guilielmi Peraldi \u8230 \'85 Summae virtutum ac vitiorum tomus I et II. Hac postrema editione \u8230 \'85 studio et opera Rodolphi \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Clutii\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . K\u246 \'f6ln 1614 (VD17 12:135421H), hier Bd. 1, S. 402-404 (mit K\u252 \'fcrzungen sowie ge\u228 \'e4nderter Reihenfolge der Numerierung). \endash \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8  (c) Wie unter (a), Sermo 9;\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  Druck: GW 7410, Bl. B4\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  B vorletzter Satz-\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 [B5]\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 va\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\chcbpat8 .}

