\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 97\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -100\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24  Ps. Thomas de Aquino: Expositio in Boethii De consolatione Philosophiae (Exz. lib. 4)
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (97\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Expositio zu Prosa 6\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 a\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Notandum quod quidam plus timent ... \endash  ... sine diuina gratia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  Expositio zu Prosa 7\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 a\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Primum exemplum est tale: Paris filius Priami regis Troianorum ... \endash  ... et per hoc caelum meruit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Ausz\u252 \'fcge aus dem Kommentar des Ps. Thomas (Guilelmus Wheatley?), s.o. 2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 rv\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Verglichen mit:GW 4556 =  BSB-Ink B-608, Bl. zIIII\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 ; X[6]\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 -X[8]\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  (Ausgabe bietet wie die Hs. Text und Kommentar getrennt voneinander).}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f2\fnil\fcharset0 Calibri;}{\f3\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 100\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -102\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 Ps. Augustinus: Epistolae
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Epistola beati Augustini ad Petrum Diaconum. Questio: Vtrum animae defunctorum notitiam habeant de charis suis qui sunt in praesenti uita et solutio. Quia prima questio, fili quam soluendam per fratrem Dorotheum nobis transmisisti presupponit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  ... \endash  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 pro quo oro.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  CPPM IIA, 203(2; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 R\u246 \'f6mer\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (wie unten)\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 ,\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  S. 129. \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (101\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Idem in quadam epistola ad Bonifacium comitem de adulatoribus. Omnis adulator hypocrita est, remissus et tepidus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  ... \endash  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 fallaciter\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . CPPM IIA, 203(4; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 R\u246 \'f6mer\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (wie unten)\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 ,\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  S. 132, Z. 43-47. \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 3\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (101\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Alia Aurelii Augustini episcopi ad Cirillum epistola \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ... (101\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Dilecto filio Cirillo Augustinus Hipponensis episcopus salutem. Tua charitate devictus mox tuis literis respondere curavi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  ... \endash  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 refundere audeamus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . CPPM IIA, 203(13; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 R\u246 \'f6mer\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (wie unten)\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 ,\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  S. 138. \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (102\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Epistola beati Augustini episcopi ad Cantianum militem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  ... (102\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Scripsisti nobis utrum delicate vestiri\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  ... (102\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 in cruce pendentem. Ora pro me.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (CPPM IIA, 203(24; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 R\u246 \'f6mer\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (wie unten)\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 ,\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Bd. 3, S. 150.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Ausz\u252 \'fcge aus einer recht verbreiteten pseudo-augustinischen Briefsammlung. Zur Sammlung: Franz \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 R\u246 \'f6mer\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , A Late Medieval Collection of Epistles Ascribed to Saint Augustine. In: Augustinian Studies 2 (1971), S. 115-154 und Bd. 3, S. 147-189; zur \u220 \'dcberlieferung der Sammlung: Bd. 2, S. 122-127.}

