\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Meditacio redempcionis humane Bernhardi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 O\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 nima\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!, vielm. Anima) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 christiana, anima de graui morte suscitata\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 quia tu es cum patre et spiritu sancto deus solus benedictus in secula seculorum. Amen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Et sic est finis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b \endash  96\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rv\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  leer.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Edition: PL 158, 762-769; S. Anselmi Cantuariensis archiepiscopi opera omnia. Bd. 3: Continens orationes sive meditationes necnon epistolarium librum primum, rec. Franciscus Salesius \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Schmitt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Edinburgh 1946, S. 84-91 (hier Meditatio 3).}

