\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 45\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 -119\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Priscianus: De constructione\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (lib. 17-18)
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Quoniam in ante expositis libris de partibus oracionis in plerisque Apollonii auctoritatem sumus secuti\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (II.107.23) \u8230 \'85 \endash  (81\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Z. 10) Kolophon: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Artis Prisciani v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [iri]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  di\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [sertissimi] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 grammatici Cesariensis doctoris vrbis Rome Constantinopolitane xvii \plain \f1\i\scaps\lang1033\fs24 liber de constrvctione explicitvs feliciter\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Druck: II.209.4-8). \endash  (81\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Z. 16) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Incipit liber xviii\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . [I]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 n\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 superiore libro de articularium dictionum et pronominum tractantes constructionibus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Ter\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [encius] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 in And\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [ria] (!, vielm. Adelphis): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 sed postquam intus sum omnium rerum satur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  Kolophon: \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Explicit strvctio Prisciani Grammatici Deo Gracias. Amen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b. \endash  Nachtrag einer Quaestio von anderer Hand: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Queritur, utrum apostolus optans aliquid, cum dixit: Optabam esse anathema\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Rm 9,3) \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 solus deus est, in quem peccatum cadere non potest; cetera, cum sint liberi arbitrii, ad utramque partem flecti possunt, ergo cum ad utramque partem flecti poterat\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Thomas de Aquino, Summa theologia I, qu. 19, art. 10).
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Druck: Prisciani \u8230 \'85 institutionum grammaticarum libri XVIII (wie oben), Bd. 2, S. 107-377. \endash  Lit.: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Bursill-Hall\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , S. 154 Nr. 176.142.3.}

