\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 98\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -104\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 Excerpta et notae
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (Z. 19) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Petri Damiani verba in uxores clericorum. Vos tigrides impie, quarum nesciunt preter humanum sanguinem, cruenta ora sitire \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 crudeliter deuorastis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Petrus Damianus, Contra intemperantes clericos, lib. 2,2, cap. 7; PL 145, 410BC). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (98\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ,vorletzte Zeile) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Tres sunt positure uel distinctiones, quas Greci thesis uocant, distinctio, subdistinctio, media distinctio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 cuius partes sunt cola et commata\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Donatus, Ars grammatica 1, cap. De posituris); (99\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Z. 13-21) Zusatz: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Coma particula est sententie, cola: membra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 sed in minori sensu, colum in maiori coma\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 3\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (99\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Quod sunt differentie in nomine\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Quod sunt differentie principales in nomine? Responditur quattuor. Que? Corporalis et incorporalis proprium et appellatiuum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 quia omnia nomina, pronomina, participia declinantur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (100\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Z. 13) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Partes grammatice artis, quod\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!, vielm. quot) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 sunt? Responditur: Prima pars est, que scribitur per metaforam et antiforam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 quomodo interrogare et respondere possent incipiens a littera\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Julianus Toletanus, Excerpta ex commentariis in Donatum, cap. De littera). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 5\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (100\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Z. 19) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Perfecta forma, quod\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!, vielm. quot) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 coniunctiones\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!, coniugationes) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 habet? Responditur: Omnes aliquando positiones, aliquando diminutiua, aliquando et omnia tempora habet\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  quibus modis interrogatur omne, quod interrogatur? Responditur: Tribus, aut probandi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  [aut temptandi] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 aut discendi.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Qualiter ostenduntur uerborum genera?\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 [Responditur:] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 D\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 uobus modis.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 6\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (100\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Z. 10) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Littera quid est? Elementum uocis articulare. Elementum quid est? Responditur: Conceptio sensus. Sensus quid est? Glomeratio cogitationis que explanatur per uocem. Uox est ante uerbum aut uerbum ante uocem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 habet diminucionem ut homuncio, humunculus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 7\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (101\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Z. 14) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Ars quid est? Rei cuiusque scientia. Arcium generationes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!, vielm. genera) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 quod\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!, vielm. quot) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 sunt? Tres\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 consuetudine eorum, que in medio loquendi usu placita adsumptaque sunt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Maximus Victorinus, De arte grammatica). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 8\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (102\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Z. 3) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Non est persona in iudicio consideranda, sed causa\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  nec cohibere a iustitia didicit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Isidorus Hispalensis, Liber sententiarum, lib. 3, cap. 53; PL 83, 726AB); (102\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Z. 13) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Si mendatium gratis dicitur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 tantum ad ministerium debet esse salutis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (ebd., cap. 55; PL 83, 727AC); (102\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Z. 17) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Qui recte iudicat et premium inde remunerationis expetit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 sepe innocentia leditur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (ebd., cap. 54; PL 83, 726B-727A). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 9\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (103\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Z. 18) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Duodecim uerba abusiua sunt seculi: Sapiens sine bonis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  [operibus] (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Walther\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Initia carminum 17280). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 10\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (103\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , vorletzte Zeile) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Quid modis dicitur ira quattuor: Primum genus ire, quod mox suscitatur et mox sanatur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 hoc vero genus e contrario insanabile est\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 11\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (103\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Z. 3) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Quatuor colunne \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (!, vielm. columne)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  sustinent homines: prudentia, fortitudo, iustitia, temperantia. Prudentia mala deuitantur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Regnum sine commutatione\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (vgl. PL 94, 545CD). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (103\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Z. 18) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Humanum genus ita diffinit Apuleius Platonicus: Homines, inquit, racione plaudentes, oracione pollentes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 cita morte, querula vita\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Apuleius Madaurensis, De deo Socratis, cap. 4; wohl nach Augustinus, De civitate dei, lib. 9, cap. 8); (104\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Z. 1) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Omnium, inquit Platonicus Apuleius, animalium, in quibus anima rationalis, tripertita diuisio est\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ita hominibus, quibus superius habitant, preferendi sunt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Augustinus, De civitate dei, lib. 8, cap. 14); (ebd., Z. 12) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Diffinit demonvm bene animali, animo passiua, mente rationalia, corpore aeria\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (ebd., cap. 16). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 13\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (104\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Z. 14) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Oportet omnibus Rethorice professoribus, ut non solvm eloquenter, sed eciam sapienter dicant \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 et ad populum proferant, si eam personam gerunt, non\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  [in]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 probrie faciunt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (vgl. Hrabanus Maurus, De clericorum institutione, lib. 3, cap. 36; PL 107, 412D-413A). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 14\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (104\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Rethorica est ratio vel copia dicendi que docet ornate verba componere, unicuique persone, etati, sexui nec non ordini et dignitati congrua accidentia distribuere, et modum et ordinem discernere\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  Rest der Seite sowie 105\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rv\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  leer.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Exzerpte aus Grammatikern sowie aus Petrus Damiani, Augustin, Isidor u.a., auch anonyme Regeln und Merkspr\u252 \'fcche. \endash  Gesamted.: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Groll\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  2, s.o. Lit., S. 109-124 (nicht eingesehen). \endash  Edition und Lit.: (Nr. 2) Probi, Donati, Servii qui feruntur de arte grammatica libri, rec. Heinrich \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Keil\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Leipzig 1864. ND Hildesheim 1961 (Grammatici latini 4), S. 372, Z. 15-23; einschlie\u223 \'dflich Zusatz auch abgedruckt in: Gian Carlo \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Alessio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , L\rquote ars dictaminis nelle scuole dell\rquote Italia meridionale (secoli XI-XIII), in: Lucidissima dictandi peritia. Studi di grammatica e retorica medievale, a cura di Filippo \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Bognini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Venedig 2015 (Filologie medievali e moderne 8. Serie occidentale 7), S. 205-222, hier S. 211. \endash  (Nr. 3) Parallel\u252 \'fcberlieferung: Paris, BNF, Lat. 2772, 76\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 -77\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . \endash  (Nr. 4) Artium scriptores minores, rec. Heinrich \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Keil\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Leipzig 1868. ND Hildesheim 1961 (Grammatici latini 5), S. 320, Z. 10-15; Ars Iuliani Toletani episcopi. Una gram\u225 \'e1tica latina de la Espa\u241 \'f1a visigoda, estudio y ed. cr\u237 \'edtica por Maria A. H. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Maestre Yenes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Toledo 1973 (Publicaciones 5), S. 113f. \endash  (Nr. 5) Nicht identifiziert. \endash  (Nr. 6) Parallel\u252 \'fcberlieferung: London, BL, Cotton Nero A.II, 33\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 -34\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 ; Lit.: Constant J. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Mews\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Apostolic Authority and Celtic Liturgies: From the \u8218 \'82Vita Samsonis\u8219 ' to the \u8218 \'82Ratio de cursus\u8219 ', in: St Samson of Dol and the Earliest History of Brittany, Cornwall and Wales, ed. by Lynette \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Olson\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Woodbridge 2017 (Studies in Celtic History 37), S. 115-135, hier S. 124, Anm. 50. \endash  (Nr. 7) Scriptores artis metricae, rec. Heinrich \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Keil\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Leipzig 1874. ND Hildesheim 1961 (Grammatici Latini 6), S. 187, Z. 1-189, Z. 7. \endash  (Nr. 10) Nicht identifiziert. \endash  (Nr. 12) Zur Vermittlung des Zitats von Apuleius Madaurensis \u252 \'fcber Augustinus vgl. Frank \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Regen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Der Codex Laurentianus pluteus 51,9. Ein bisher vernachl\u228 \'e4ssigter Textzeuge der Apuleischen Schrift \u8218 \'82De deo Socratis\u8219 '. G\u246 \'f6ttingen 1985 (Nachrichten der Akademie der Wissenschaften zu G\u246 \'f6ttingen, Phil.-Hist. Kl. 1985,5, S. 195-238, hier S. 204, Anm. 21. \endash  (Nr. 14) Abgedruckt in: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Alessio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , L\rquote ars dictaminis (s. Nr. 2), S. 207.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 106\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Besitzeintrag, dreizeilig, auf Rasur: Z. 2 m\u246 \'f6glicherweise: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Iste liber\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85, Rest auch mit UV-Licht nicht lesbar.}

