\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 128\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 -131\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Nota et schemata
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (129\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  letzte Zeile) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Congaudet autem veritati, quia, ut se ceteros\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (mit Verweisungszeichen, Beginn des Zitats auf 128\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  vorletzte Zeile) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 diligens per hoc, quod rectum in aliis conspicit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 quia,\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 quod sola dileccione erga omnes inhiat, in perdicione aduersancium non exultat\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (129\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Bernhardus. Maledictum caput tremulum et cor emulum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 anni multi et actus stulti\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 3\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Magister in sentenciis libro i distinccione iii. Ambrosius ait, ut deus quia in natura invisibilis est, eciam a visibilibus posset sciri \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 humana mens cognoscere potuit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (130\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Sacerdos quidam secularis quadam die missam celebraret, alius ei assistens\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 cum summa velocitate illabi in os sacerdotis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 5\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Oracio est homini necessaria ex eo, quod est nunccius eius, quem homo mittit ad deum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ne nimis lasciuiant Eph. vi: State subcincti\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 (Eph 6,14). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 6\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (130\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Bernhardus: Caro mea de luto est, ideo lutosas cogitaciones ab ea habeo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 (PL 184, 504C); daran: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Wersus: Nos vexant triplici certamine tres inimici\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Walther\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Proverbia 18807). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 7\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Exemplum bonum de confessione. Sanctus Thomas, cum iam deberet mori, vidit dyabolum stantem ante se \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 statim liber et mobilis sit ad bonum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 8\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Nota bene: Melius esset quod triginta viri, qui conspirassent omnes in necem tuam, starent super te eductis cultris \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 9\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Wersus: Hec sunt sanctorum pia nomina munere quorum | Mens afflictorum letatur fine bonorum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ... \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 10\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Silencium \endash  letificat hominem \endash  Psalmus \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [106,30] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Letati sunt, quia siluerunt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 11\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (131\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Wersus: Ora, scribe, stude, dormi, lege vel meditare \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Walther\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Proverbia 20336). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Considera \endash  beneficia dei ut deuotus et gratus \endash  septem lucerne candelabri \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 13\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Jhesus docet nos cum \endash  leccionis meditacionis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!, meditatio geh\u246 \'f6rt zu Zeile 2 des Schemas) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 \endash  exercicio \endash  abstinenciam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ; \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 meditacionis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 exercicio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 continenciam \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 14\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Jhesus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  [est] \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Opifex sapientissimus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 15\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 In contemplacione mens \endash  delectatur \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 16\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Jhesus fuit fortis \endash  in adgrediendo \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 17\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Jhesus factus est nobis \endash  Sapiencia \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 18\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Wersus: Sic transformatur cor amantis, in id quod amatur \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Walther\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Proverbia 29553). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 19\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Gregorius: Quamuis cogitacio siue delectatio quantumcumque immunda mentem non coinquinat \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 (PL 184, 674B). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 20\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Jeronimus: Siue legis siue scribis siue dormis siue vigiles \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 (PL 22, 644f.). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 21\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (131\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Deus dicitur cunctipotens\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Deus est omnipotens, quia potest omnia que w\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [u]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 lt. Psalmus: Omnia quecumque voluit, dominus fecit in celo et in terra, in mari et in omnibus abissis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Ps 134,6) \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 sed cucurrit, quia accurrens cecidit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 (Nr. 1) Druck: Johannes \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Marbach\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Geschichte der deutschen Predigt vor Luther. Bd. 1, erste H\u228 \'e4lfte. Berlin 1874, S. 31-34 (mit Umstellungen und Auslassungen). \endash  (Nr. 2) Zitiert nach Felix Hemmerlin, Dialogus de nobilitate et rusticitate, cap. 2; Druck: GW 12189, Bl. a[8]\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , vorletzte Zeile-a[8]\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Z. 3. \endash  (Nr. 3) Druck: Thomas von Aquin. Texte zum Gottesbeweis, hrsg. von Engelbert \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Krebs\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Bonn 1921 (Kleine Texte f\u252 \'fcr Vorlesungen und \u220 \'dcbungen 91), S. 4, Z. 15-S. 5, Z. 3. \endash  (Nr. 4) Speculum exemplorum, dist. 9, exemplum 190; Druck: verglichen mit GW M42959 = BSB-Ink S-507, Bl. M4\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 va\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . \endash  (Nr. 5) Jacobus de Voragine, Dom. 5 post Pascha, Sermo 2, verglichen mit GW M11673 = BSB-Ink I-112, Bd. 1, Bl. k1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 va\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Z. 38-k1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Z. 12. \endash  (Nr. 7) Caesarius Heisterbacensis, Dialogus miraculorum, dist. 11, cap. 38; Druck: Caesarii Heisterbacensis Monachi ordinis Cisterciensis Dialogus, Bde. 1-2, ed. Joseph \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Strange\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , hier Bd. 2, S. 299f. \endash  (Nr. 8-9) Parallel\u252 \'fcberlieferung: Clm 14739, 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . \endash  (Nr. 10-20) Parallel\u252 \'fcberlieferung: Clm 14739, 298\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 rv\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . \endash  (Nr. 21) Jacobus de Voragine, De sancta trinitate, sermo 1, verglichen mit GW M11673 = BSB-Ink I-112, Bd. 1, Bl. l2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Z. 8-l2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 va\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Z. 41 (mit Auslassungen).}

