\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 In der Kopfzeile: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Galatas 5\u176 \'b0 Omnis lex\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Gal 5,14). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Adolescentibus tria sunt predicanda, ut fugiant mulieris familiaritatem, vt vitent lingue verbositatem, vt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  [non] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 exercentur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 inobediencie fastuositatem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!) \u8230 \'85 \endash  (168\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Z. 19) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 De penitudine autem inobediencie exemplum habemus in ipso filio Lucrecii, de quo narrat Boecius de disciplina scolarium, quod fuit absque disciplina nutritus, consumens sua in aleis et meretriciis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  ... \endash  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 filiorum patri necesse est castigacioni indulgere\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (vgl. PL 64, 1227CD; Pseudo-Bo\u232 \'e8ce: De disciplina scolarium, \u233 \'e9d. crit., introd. et notes par Olga \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Weijers\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . Leiden 1976, cap. 2 \u167 \'a7 8-9, S. 101, Z. 17-S. 102, Z. 7).}

