\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 140\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 -143\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Excerpta theologica
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 In der Kopfzeile: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Crisostomus in vi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [tam] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Christi capitulo 14\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Crisostomus. Sicut sacerdotum princepes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 sunt apostoli, sic monachorum princeps Johannes baptista est. Considerate monachi dignitatem vestram, Johannes princeps vestri est dogmatis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 quid enim prodest, si in habitacione silencium, in habitatoribus sit viciorum tumultus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (141\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Minime pro certo bonus est, qui melior esse non uult\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Hec Bernhardus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (PL 182, 224A). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 3\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (141\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) In der Kopfzeile: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Petrus Ravennatis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Juxta sentencia cordis mei, si paradisus in hac vita presenti est uel in claustro vel in scola est\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  (Z. 7) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Vnde Hugo. Nichil in hac vita dulcius sentitur, nichil auidius sumitur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 (PL 184, 498C). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 4\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Nota decem precepta moralia Sibille: Noli habere societatem cum homine, quem non noscis \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 In omnibus factis esto consultus et considera principium, medium et finem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 5\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (142\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Drei Distichen: a. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Omnis amor cecus, non est amor arbiter equus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Walther\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Proverbia 20188; TPMA 7, S. 425.391\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 ). \endash  b. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8 Sunt tria gaudia: pax, sapiencia, copia rerum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat8  (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Walther\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Initia carminum 18880; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Walther\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Proverbia 30834). \endash  c. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Lana, nemus, miles, nauigatio, rus, medicina\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Walther\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Initia carminum 10098; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Thorndike/Kibre\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  808\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 6\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Roma potens, veneranda Ravenna, Britannia nobilis, India fertilis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 7\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (142\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Augustinus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 In tribus consistit ordinacio bonorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 In estimando bonum de quolibet\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 8\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Bernhardus. Caue aliene conuersacionis, esse curiosus explorator aut temerarius iudex\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 puta ignoranciam, puta subrepcionem, puta casum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (PL 183, 984B) \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Si nullum aliud peccatum nobis fuisset admissum, pro hoc solo iehenne nos tradi satis habundeque sufficeret\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (PL 103, 616C). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 9\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (143\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Jeronimus. Magnum est demonibus a lesione cessare propter odium\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 quod contra nos habent. Et tanto grauius dimittunt, quanto diucius possiderent\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 (vgl. PL 103, 616C). Rest der Seite leer. \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 10\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (143\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) a. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Magis operando quis proficit, quam loquendo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 et omni hora tocius temporis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  b. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Bernhardus. Lingua magniloqua et manus ociosa, doctrina lucida et vita tenebrosa, monstruosa res est\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  c. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Crisostomus. Docere et non facere, non solum nichil lucri \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 vitam vero suam atque opera negligenti\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 11\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Fulgencius. Vt in celo thesaurisemus, celestia diligamus \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 et amorem tuum indicio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!, vielm. indicium) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 tue cogitacionis intelligas\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (PL 65, 724A). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Beda. Sermo doctoris in potestate fit, cum ea que docet operatur \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85 (PL 92, \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 379A).
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 (Nr. 1) Ludolphus de Saxonia, Vita Christi, pars 1, cap. 14; Druck: Vita Jesu Christi e Quatuor Evangeliis et Scriptoribus Orthodoxis Concinnata per Ludolphum de Saxonia ex Ordine Carthusianorum, studio et opera Clovis \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Bolard\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  / Louis-Marie \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Rigollot\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  / Jean Baptiste \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Carnandet\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Rom/Paris 1865, S. 70a, Z. 51-70b, Z. 49. \endash  (Nr. 4) Parallel\u252 \'fcberlieferung: Frankfurt/Main, UB J. C. Senckenberg, Ms. Praed. 121, 158\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 ; Mainz, StadtB, Hs I 307, 108\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . \endash  (Nr. 6) Vgl. Wilhelm \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Wattenbach\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Die Anf\u228 \'e4nge lateinischer profaner Rythmen des Mittelalters, in: Zeitschrift f\u252 \'fcr deutsches Alterthum und deutsche Literatur 15 (1872), S. 469-506, hier S. 502. \endash  (Nr. 7) Ludolphus de Saxonia, Vita Christi, pars 1, cap. 39; Druck, s. Nr. 1: S. 180b, Z. 3-6. \endash  (Nr. 10) Ludolphus de Saxonia, Vita Christi, pars 1, cap. 34; Druck, s. Nr. 1: a. S. 155a, Z. 5-11; b. Z. 16-19; c. S. 155b, Z. 17-21.}

